From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:05:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820-beyond2lte: Describe the whole
 panel

The boot framebuffer was described 32 pixels narrower on each side, because
the text console cannot offset its own area and its outermost columns
landed on the curve of this panel.

What runs on this phone now is an on-screen keyboard, and it wants the
opposite: its background should reach the curved edges so that no black
stripe is left there, while the keys themselves stay clear of them.  A
program cannot paint outside the buffer this node describes, so the node
describes the panel as it physically is and the program keeps its own
margin.

The memory does not change; only the window on it does.  The start moves
back to where the first boot loader puts it, the width becomes the one the
line length already said.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts | 21 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
index 6f81f18c2c3..457a133006a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
@@ -70,18 +70,21 @@ chosen {
 		 * the boot loader itself passes on this phone: the vendor kernel
 		 * receives "s3cfb.bootloaderfb=0xca000000" on its command line.
 		 */
-		framebuffer0: framebuffer@ca000080 {
+		framebuffer0: framebuffer@ca000000 {
 			compatible = "simple-framebuffer";
 			/*
-			 * The panel curves along both long edges, so the outermost
-			 * columns are distorted and hard to hit with a finger.  The
-			 * text console cannot offset its own area, so the buffer is
-			 * described 32 pixels narrower on each side instead: the
-			 * start moves by that many pixels and the line length stays
-			 * as the hardware has it.
+			 * The panel curves along both long edges.  The buffer used to
+			 * be described 32 pixels narrower on each side, because the
+			 * text console cannot offset its own area and its outermost
+			 * columns landed on the curve.  What runs on this phone now is
+			 * an on-screen keyboard that wants the opposite: it fills the
+			 * curved edges with its own background and keeps the keys
+			 * themselves clear of them.  A program cannot paint outside
+			 * the buffer this node describes, so the node describes the
+			 * panel as it physically is.
 			 */
-			reg = <0x0 0xca000080 ((1440 * 3040 - 32) * 4)>;
-			width = <1376>;
+			reg = <0x0 0xca000000 (1440 * 3040 * 4)>;
+			width = <1440>;
 			height = <3040>;
 			stride = <(1440 * 4)>;
 			format = "a8r8g8b8";
